  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sally_W24_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Sally
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7733d16353c0fcf4b99b8f89f3ad1780, type: 3}
  dialogueText: 'Adda dagiti oras a kayatmo a dumawat iti tulong iti naurnos ken
    naayat a wagas.


    Iti Ilokano, ti ''mabalin kadi a tulunganak?'' ket kayatna
    a saoen ti ''can you help me?''


    Nasayaat daytoy no kayatmo a dumawat iti
    tulong ti maysa a tao iti naurnos a wagas.


    Denggem a naimbag: mabalin kadi
    a tulunganak?


    Ita, padasem nga ibagam ti ''mabalin kadi a tulunganak?''
    iti bukodmo a timek.'
  translatedText: 'Sometimes you want to ask for help more politely.

    In Ilokano,
    ''mabalin kadi a tulunganak?'' means ''can you help me?''

    This is useful
    when politely requesting someone''s assistance.

    Now, try saying ''mabalin
    kadi a tulongannak'' yourself.'
